-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith#post1248178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from the official nuWW Facebook, apparently they are considering a new edition of Wraith after Wr20...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/39344519_10214824676202935_4306512743617265664_n.jpg?_nc_cat=0&amp;oh=3b5946d252432ec3c203627ab2b9ae39&amp;oe=5C0D242A\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oh boy, I can't wait to hear their explanation of how the Underworld/Dark Kingdoms come back from being magick-nuked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IF we assume every 2 years between lines... so 2020 werewolf, 2022 Mage, so... 2024?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T18:37:23-07:00","id":1248267,"title":"","content":"Please, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T01:26:52-07:00","id":1249642,"title":"","content":"I'm quite annoyed with ww for taking this approach to cashing in on onyx paths work to keep WoD going .I certainly won't be buying any of their products","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T01:47:18-07:00","id":1249645,"title":"","content":"I am really looking forward to a new edition of Wraith <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> To me that post is some fantastic news ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7336-teylen","name":"Teylen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T02:01:51-07:00","id":1249647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1249642#post1249642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite annoyed with ww for taking this approach to cashing in on onyx paths work to keep WoD going.</div> </div> </div> </div>...wouldn't they have already received money to begin with?<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> So yeah...they probably are going to do some retconning with the spirit-nuke. Since in WoD5e didn't retcon the Week of Nightmares, however, it probably won't be completely removing that it happened. At best, just that it didn't do as much damage to result in completely destroying the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Now the funny thing being that the sweeping changes made to the setting in V5...some of them would make more sense<br /> <br /> Dramatically changing the wraith factions. While I've only just started with Wraith as of Wr20, I'm left with the impression that no one is as...attached to the Hierarchy, Renegades, and Heretics the same way people are to the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Sabbat. So the idea of, say, the Hierarchy being in complete shambles but Renegades and Heretics having even more power is more palatable.<br /> <br /> Cities/necropoli being more cut off and isolated. From my read through in Wr20 corebook, I'm left with the impression that the necropoli generally keep to themselves and didn't talk a lot to other nearby necropoli. That they generally kept to themselves doing their own thing. So an individual necropolis being on their own makes more sense.<br /> <br /> And in the end, fresh wraiths have to go SOMEWHERE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T14:53:32-07:00","id":1250075,"title":"","content":"REALLY curious to see how they modify the different lines with the 5th edition model to the rules. In particular, I'm curious to see how they handle the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T07:52:40-07:00","id":1251915,"title":"","content":"Hunger Dice are basically a modified form of Shadow Dice but without the benefit. I hope they keep Shadow Dice as is.<br /> <br /> A setting either post- or during the Sixth Great Maelstrom might be very interesting. I always thought The Great War was produced to give us a clue to how death might be during or after the 6GM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-06-2018, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T09:42:36-07:00","id":1251937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1251915#post1251915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunger Dice are basically a modified form of Shadow Dice but without the benefit. I hope they keep Shadow Dice as is.<br /> <br /> A setting either post- or during the Sixth Great Maelstrom might be very interesting. I always thought The Great War was produced to give us a clue to how death might be during or after the 6GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd like a newer take on how to handle the Shadow that is more mechanically based. Not to say I want to take away from the RP of the Shadow, and I like the Shadow as it is, but I've had too many players that feel intimidated by the idea of needing a Shadow Guide that it would help with getting more players if I didn't have to worry about that. Wr20 gave a suggestion for it but I think even that is more of a bandaid than a solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T01:25:21-07:00","id":1252695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1251937#post1251937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd like a newer take on how to handle the Shadow that is more mechanically based. Not to say I want to take away from the RP of the Shadow, and I like the Shadow as it is, but I've had too many players that feel intimidated by the idea of needing a Shadow Guide that it would help with getting more players if I didn't have to worry about that. Wr20 gave a suggestion for it but I think even that is more of a bandaid than a solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadowguide is sort of integral to the game, though. It's easy enough to hand those duties over to the Storyteller if players don't want to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T18:19:31-07:00","id":1253442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1249647#post1249647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cities/necropoli being more cut off and isolated. From my read through in Wr20 corebook, I'm left with the impression that the necropoli generally keep to themselves and didn't talk a lot to other nearby necropoli. That they generally kept to themselves doing their own thing. So an individual necropolis being on their own makes more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a leak (since a dev has already sketched the book's outline) to say that Book of Oblivion will include some interesting and varied Necropoli.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1251915#post1251915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A setting either post- or during the Sixth Great Maelstrom might be very interesting. I always thought The Great War was produced to give us a clue to how death might be during or after the 6GM.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Hmm</i>.<br /> <br /> - C.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T21:08:20-07:00","id":1259917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1248197#post1248197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are great news, but I'm still holding my breath on seeing what they are going to do for Mage without Phil Brucato (who, as far as I know, is not working with White Wolf). Additionally, will this open the doors for a new edition of Changeling: the Dreaming?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not as knowledgeable on Mage history, but weren\u2019t they always switching Authors and Developers Around? I did like how they handled Revised era, and I liked the further meta plot in M20, with the reshuffled factions, and new faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T21:34:34-07:00","id":1259920,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, as for Changeling...<br /> <br /> At least going by the Walking Away from Arcadia podcast's, the hosts apparently caught the ear of a nuWW dev (I think it was Ericcson) saying that the upcoming blockbuster LARP &quot;Atlantic City Dreams&quot; they were going to use to test and gauge interest in Changeling (I don't think if it was made clear if it was in terms of creative direction or just &quot;are there enough Changeling fans to make this a thing&quot;), and that in the dev's eyes, changelings are &quot;the outsiders of WoD&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T03:47:30-07:00","id":1259942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1259920#post1259920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, as for Changeling...<br /> <br /> At least going by the Walking Away from Arcadia podcast's, the hosts apparently caught the ear of a nuWW dev (I think it was Ericcson) saying that the upcoming blockbuster LARP &quot;Atlantic City Dreams&quot; they were going to use to test and gauge interest in Changeling (I don't think if it was made clear if it was in terms of creative direction or just &quot;are there enough Changeling fans to make this a thing&quot;), and that in the dev's eyes, changelings are &quot;the outsiders of WoD&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope to god its not in terms of creative direction...that LARP is....'special'...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T13:07:56-07:00","id":1261151,"title":"","content":"I don't think LARPs are a good way to gauge engagement in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T11:22:28-07:00","id":1262557,"title":"","content":"Is White Wolf pulling away from Onyx? Onyx just released Wraith 20th and suddenly White Wolf wants to do a new one already? What's up with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22337-overcastghost","name":"OvercastGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22337_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T19:30:25-07:00","id":1262617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OvercastGhost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1262557#post1262557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is White Wolf pulling away from Onyx? Onyx just released Wraith 20th and suddenly White Wolf wants to do a new one already? What's up with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that OPP's Kickstarter for Chicago by Night V5 is a week away, I doubt it.<br /> <br /> I caught a tidbit online how nuWW plans to bring in new editions for EVERY WoD gameline. It's just that the timeline of when those new editions will come out is a bit unclear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T19:51:28-07:00","id":1262619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OvercastGhost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1262557#post1262557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is White Wolf pulling away from Onyx? Onyx just released Wraith 20th and suddenly White Wolf wants to do a new one already? What's up with that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They've said that they want to do a 5e-equivalent version of all the WoD lines. But none of that is 'near future'. Last they said they're finishing up the current Vampire books and working on Werewolf and Sabbat for down the line. Chill, it's not like they're going to be doing anything like, next year with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T14:59:09-07:00","id":1262948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OvercastGhost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1248178-nu-white-wolf-considering-a-new-edition-of-wraith?p=1262557#post1262557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is White Wolf pulling away from Onyx? Onyx just released Wraith 20th and suddenly White Wolf wants to do a new one already? What's up with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering the actual 20th Anniversary of Wraith: The Oblivion's original release would have been 2014, we may have an answer to that! The 20th Anniversary book was late, and only just made it into the typical cycle of new editions.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I wouldn't worry about it. I still have all my 20th Anniversary books, but I am still enjoying the direction of V5. Wraith will get an update in due course - maybe in about 3 years at a guess. There is also the complication that, outside of the 'big three' (Vampire, Werewolf, Mage), White Wolf may wish to do other games too. I could, for example, see a good argument for them taking cues from Chronicles of Darkness to make their own versions of Hunter (the Second Inquisition?) or Promethean, before they get round to Wraith. So, potentially, the new Wraith edition could be even further out, and they may even want to change it in some way from the format we have now.<br /> <br /> That gives plenty of fresh playtime to use the Wr20 book well, and then you could hold on to it as a collector, or sell it if you prefer, or just ignore Wr5 when it comes about. Personally, I think Wr20 is wonderful and will be something I will hold on to - but I am willing to see what comes next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}